# LaTeX: Theorem Environments

## Theorem Environments

Theorem environments provide a way to automatically number equations and theorems. The following environments are defined by AMS-LaTeX:

• \newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}
• \newtheorem{lemma}{Lemma}
• \newtheorem{corollary}{Corollary}
• \newtheorem{definition}{Definition}
• \newtheorem{example}{Example}

The first parameter is the name of the environment and the second one the name to be printed.

Note that the actual text (Theorem, Lemma, ect.) is printed in boldface and that the line breaks (\\) in the second argument of \newtheorem are only there to save print space. The breaks will not result in line breaks.

The environments themselves work as follows:

\begin{theorem}
This is the statement of the theorem.
\end{theorem}

The numbering of equations and theorems can be disabled by means of the starred environment.

## Theorem Styles

The numbering style for theorems can be set with the \newtheoremstyle command. The following styles are defined:

• \newtheoremstyle{plain}
• \newtheoremstyle{definition}
• \newtheoremstyle

